WEBVTT

00:01.020 --> 00:06.120
At the hospital, you will be apprenticed 
under a doctor named Graham.

00:06.120 --> 00:10.290
If I remember correctly, he's a genius
and the youngest instructor there.

00:10.290 --> 00:13.480
<i>To think I'll have the chance to learn 
medicine from someone like that!</i>

00:13.480 --> 00:15.410
I was wondering, Father,

00:15.410 --> 00:19.930
did you hide the fact that I'm your 
daughter like I hoped you would?

00:19.930 --> 00:24.170
Yes, I told them you'd been 
recommended by Viscount Kait.

00:24.170 --> 00:28.430
But why are you hiding the fact that 
you're from the Clorence family?

00:28.780 --> 00:31.100
You're even using the
name Rose as a pseudonym.

00:31.330 --> 00:33.530
If they learn that I'm your daughter,

00:33.530 --> 00:36.100
they won't treat me the way 
they do everyone else.

00:39.220 --> 00:40.650
Is something wrong?

00:41.010 --> 00:44.130
Lise, you're going to a relief 
hospital for the poor, aren't you?

00:44.130 --> 00:46.780
I'm worried that you'll have 
a difficult time there.

00:46.780 --> 00:50.560
Yes, I think I'll sneak in from time 
 to time to see how you're faring.

00:50.560 --> 00:52.820
Th-There's no need to do that!

00:52.820 --> 00:54.520
You don't have to worry.

00:54.740 --> 00:58.010
Really? Well, just don't 
push yourself too hard.

00:58.470 --> 01:00.910
It's too late to do anything 
after you've ruined your health.

01:01.370 --> 01:05.280
Elise, if anything happens, 
come and tell me immediately.

01:05.510 --> 01:08.010
I will! Thank you!

01:14.170 --> 01:15.650
<i>Teresa Hospital.</i>

01:16.450 --> 01:19.210
<i>I have to earn my license 
here as quickly as possible...</i>

01:21.190 --> 01:23.620
<i>and win my wager with His Majesty!</i>

02:54.900 --> 02:57.400
Leaving a girl like this to me...

02:58.200 --> 03:00.980
Do they think a hospital is 
some sort of ball?

03:01.740 --> 03:04.490
If you're even one minute late
 for our ten 'o clock appointment...

03:05.050 --> 03:06.660
I'll throw you out on the spot.

03:20.850 --> 03:24.960
I'm honored to meet you. My name is Rose.

03:27.710 --> 03:31.960
<i>From her appearance, she's a typical 
example of a young noblewoman.</i>

03:32.440 --> 03:33.410
Excuse me...

03:34.320 --> 03:36.680
Are you Doctor Graham?

03:36.680 --> 03:40.230
Huh? Yes, I'm Graham.

03:40.600 --> 03:42.340
I heard you want to be a doctor.

03:42.340 --> 03:43.220
I do.

03:44.290 --> 03:47.260
You're not old enough to have 
graduated from the academy.

03:47.800 --> 03:49.990
How have you been studying medicine?

03:50.270 --> 03:52.090
I taught myself.

03:52.880 --> 03:54.450
Did you say you taught yourself?

03:57.020 --> 04:01.590
<i>If this weren't a request from Viscount 
Kait, I'd throw her out right now.</i>

04:02.710 --> 04:04.970
Do you understand what the healing arts are?

04:04.970 --> 04:05.730
Yes.

04:06.140 --> 04:08.550
It's about treating and curing patients.

04:09.000 --> 04:14.670
Then, if it so happened that a patient lost 
their life while undergoing treatment,

04:15.420 --> 04:16.660
what would you do?

04:22.260 --> 04:25.620
I would carve it into my heart.

04:29.650 --> 04:33.420
<i>She's like a doctor who has faced 
patients' deaths many times.</i>

04:36.000 --> 04:39.620
Doctor, what work will I be doing?

04:39.620 --> 04:40.480
Huh?

04:40.480 --> 04:42.630
Oh. I'll explain.

04:42.630 --> 04:43.620
Follow me.

04:49.660 --> 04:52.310
This is where you'll be working from now on.

04:52.870 --> 04:54.970
And these patients?

04:54.970 --> 04:57.000
They're all people without families.

04:57.000 --> 04:59.060
Patients with severe illnesses

04:59.510 --> 05:03.310
and patients that are beyond 
our aid stay in this ward.

05:04.500 --> 05:07.190
What treatments will I be giving them?

05:07.610 --> 05:10.480
Will I be treating their underlying conditions?

05:10.480 --> 05:14.940
Or will I be alleviating their symptoms 
through conservative treatments?

05:15.360 --> 05:17.980
<i>Her questions are right on the mark.</i>

05:17.980 --> 05:19.660
<i>Is it just a coincidence?</i>

05:20.540 --> 05:23.200
Do whatever's within your 
capabilities for them.

05:23.200 --> 05:26.920
But don't go blundering ahead 
if you don't know what to do.

05:27.220 --> 05:29.800
Yes, sir. I understand.

05:33.910 --> 05:36.730
<i>It might be cruel to place her there,</i>

05:36.730 --> 05:39.910
<i>but if she's going to quit anyway, it's 
better to make her realize it sooner.</i>

05:40.610 --> 05:43.250
<i>She'll likely only last a few days at most.</i>

05:44.870 --> 05:47.440
Just look at her and her frilly clothes.

05:47.440 --> 05:49.230
She's like a little princess.

05:49.490 --> 05:51.860
Miss, may I ask who you are?

05:51.860 --> 05:53.540
My name is Rose.

05:53.540 --> 05:56.380
I'm starting here today as an apprentice. 
I look forward to your help.

05:56.860 --> 05:59.710
What can a child like her do anyway?

06:02.250 --> 06:04.840
May I borrow some cleaning implements?

06:04.840 --> 06:06.620
Y-Yes.

06:12.060 --> 06:14.560
If we make sure to keep things 
as hygienic as possible,

06:14.560 --> 06:16.890
we can reduce the mortality rate!

06:22.740 --> 06:27.040
No one has done any cleaning here before.

06:28.210 --> 06:30.900
She says it's for the patients, but still...

06:42.150 --> 06:44.230
Doing all that alone must be hard.

06:48.770 --> 06:49.880
Ahem.

07:10.900 --> 07:13.320
It's so clean now, I wouldn't 
have recognized it!

07:13.570 --> 07:17.120
Yes, and it's all thanks to your help!

07:17.120 --> 07:20.230
Your clothes have gotten quite soiled.

07:20.230 --> 07:23.450
Please don't worry. This is 
part of the job, after all.

07:24.770 --> 07:26.080
It hurts...

07:27.930 --> 07:31.080
This guy was fixing a roof and fell.

07:31.350 --> 07:33.430
He broke a rib.

07:34.470 --> 07:36.960
Please let me look at it for a moment.

07:44.750 --> 07:47.170
<i>He's been lying down so long,
 he's developed bedsores.</i>

07:47.720 --> 07:49.600
<i>It's become quite serious.</i>

07:50.830 --> 07:52.730
Please take him to a treatment room.

07:52.730 --> 07:53.370
What?

07:53.650 --> 07:55.630
If we leave him in this state,

07:55.630 --> 07:58.960
it may lead to an infection
 and blood poisoning.

07:59.290 --> 08:01.700
Please bring me disinfectant solution,

08:01.700 --> 08:03.740
anesthetic, and a scalpel from the pharmacy.

08:03.740 --> 08:04.810
A scalpel?

08:04.810 --> 08:07.120
Are you saying you'll be performing surgery?

08:07.120 --> 08:08.700
You, miss?

08:08.700 --> 08:11.800
Yes. I will remove the 
dead sections of skin.

08:11.800 --> 08:15.850
There's a possibility of heavy bleeding, 
so please bring gauze as well.

08:17.610 --> 08:19.640
This is just crazy.

08:19.640 --> 08:20.340
Yeah.

08:20.690 --> 08:21.990
Is it gonna be all right?

08:21.990 --> 08:23.360
If she makes a mistake...

08:27.360 --> 08:29.330
I want to help you.

08:41.320 --> 08:44.640
<i>I wonder if Doctor Graham 
will scold me later.</i>

08:45.520 --> 08:46.240
<i>But...</i>

08:47.320 --> 08:50.610
<i>I can't just stand aside when a 
patient's condition has worsened.</i>

08:56.090 --> 08:59.040
The anesthetic is working, 
so this shouldn't hurt.

08:59.590 --> 09:03.080
It's all right. The surgery 
will be over quickly.

09:05.790 --> 09:07.510
Disinfectant, please.

09:07.510 --> 09:08.830
Y-Yes.

09:18.570 --> 09:19.810
Scalpel, please.

09:22.440 --> 09:23.840
Quickly, please.

09:24.120 --> 09:25.090
Yes.

09:31.270 --> 09:35.010
<i>This is the first time I've held a 
scalpel since becoming Elise again.</i>

09:36.660 --> 09:37.580
<i>But...</i>

09:39.840 --> 09:43.390
<i>I have more than enough experience 
from my time as Takamoto Aoi.</i>

09:44.220 --> 09:46.530
<i>So everything will be all right.</i>

09:48.770 --> 09:50.350
I will now begin the surgery.

10:13.430 --> 10:15.790
Please prepare a dressing.

10:16.290 --> 10:18.270
We will use it to cover the wound.

10:18.270 --> 10:19.260
Right away!

10:31.900 --> 10:34.820
I think you've even got 
more color in your face!

10:34.820 --> 10:38.520
Thank you, miss. I feel 
a whole lot better now.

10:38.520 --> 10:42.550
Of course! But we still need to monitor you.

10:42.550 --> 10:45.360
If you notice anything, 
please tell me right away.

10:47.460 --> 10:49.380
I was just so happy.

10:50.700 --> 10:52.900
Whenever I showed any anxiety,

10:52.900 --> 10:57.130
Miss Rose told me I'd be 
all right over and over.

10:57.620 --> 11:02.130
It's been a long time since 
anyone was that kind to me.

11:05.090 --> 11:09.380
I-I just did what any doctor should do.

11:09.670 --> 11:10.400
All right!

11:10.400 --> 11:13.050
I want Miss Rose to treat me, too!

11:13.050 --> 11:17.470
Hang on! You basically just have a 
scratch! My treatment comes first.

11:17.470 --> 11:19.150
Yours is just a scratch, too!

11:19.150 --> 11:20.110
Then, I'll go.

11:20.110 --> 11:21.030
No, I'm next!

11:21.030 --> 11:23.080
You go by who's oldest at times like these!

11:23.080 --> 11:26.640
I'm next! Oldest first! Yours 
isn't even that serious!

11:25.150 --> 11:28.150
E-Everyone, please calm down!

11:28.910 --> 11:30.350
Um...

11:30.350 --> 11:33.290
Will you help me with the next 
patient's treatment, too?

11:35.270 --> 11:36.330
Of course!

11:38.420 --> 11:40.010
Thank you!

11:44.370 --> 11:46.690
Why can't you identify the disease?

11:47.210 --> 11:48.990
I'm very sorry.

11:48.990 --> 11:51.130
You're the best doctor in 
the empire, aren't you?

11:51.130 --> 11:52.690
Don't reproach him so harshly.

11:53.730 --> 11:57.190
Viscount Ven says he 
doesn't know what it is,

11:57.550 --> 12:01.580
which only shows how difficult 
my illness must be to treat.

12:07.400 --> 12:09.460
Recently, a certain person said...

12:10.730 --> 12:14.460
that when the concentration of 
sugar in the blood increases

12:14.460 --> 12:17.780
symptoms like these often appear.

12:18.220 --> 12:19.970
Do you know anything about that?

12:22.150 --> 12:25.550
<i>Previously, the medical association of the 
Republic of Fresgard</i>

12:25.550 --> 12:28.480
<i>made a presentation about such an illness,</i>

12:29.150 --> 12:34.430
<i>but there are fewer than twenty people, 
including me, who know about it.</i>

12:34.430 --> 12:36.850
Do you have some idea what it might be?

12:37.150 --> 12:40.270
Yes, though I can't be 
absolutely certain yet.

12:41.160 --> 12:45.770
Your Highness, what doctor 
mentioned this condition to you?

12:45.770 --> 12:48.840
That person is undoubtedly 
an extraordinary physician!

12:48.840 --> 12:50.490
No, it was—

12:50.720 --> 12:54.090
It isn't important who 
he heard it from, is it?

12:55.080 --> 12:58.890
Treating His Majesty's illness 
takes precedence right now.

12:59.550 --> 13:02.780
If you've found some clue, then go 
and investigate it immediately.

13:02.780 --> 13:04.440
Understood.

13:09.280 --> 13:13.320
Why did you hide the fact 
that it was Lady Elise?

13:13.320 --> 13:15.500
There is no need to entangle

13:15.500 --> 13:18.480
our future crown princess 
with the medical association.

13:18.480 --> 13:22.950
In truth, she should be made to quit the 
hospital and return here immediately.

13:24.450 --> 13:28.810
Leaving that aside, how 
fares the Kusef campaign?

13:29.240 --> 13:32.430
The second corps is advancing 
toward the Kusef Peninsula.

13:32.430 --> 13:35.580
They should be able to penetrate 
the peninsula in a few days.

13:36.020 --> 13:37.330
The other day,

13:37.330 --> 13:41.350
Lady Elise mentioned the Kingdom of 
Moncelle. What are their movements?

13:41.350 --> 13:47.830
An envoy from the Republic of Fresgard 
has made frequent visits of late.

13:48.050 --> 13:50.730
What? Is that true?

13:51.860 --> 13:55.220
Our intelligence bureau verified it. 
The information is accurate.

13:55.530 --> 13:57.290
It seems that after the envoy's visit,

13:57.290 --> 14:00.970
the Kingdom of Moncelle's military 
secretly began to mobilize.

14:01.270 --> 14:04.110
It seems to be a plan to take our rear.

14:04.380 --> 14:05.690
I see.

14:06.520 --> 14:10.570
If we hadn't learned this, I wonder 
how we would be faring now.

14:11.260 --> 14:15.610
Lady Elise has saved our empire.

14:20.670 --> 14:22.470
What are you thinking?

14:22.470 --> 14:24.670
A week of independent study?

14:24.670 --> 14:27.630
She wasn't referred by just anyone. 
It was Viscount Kait!

14:28.350 --> 14:29.880
My deepest apologies.

14:29.880 --> 14:32.130
Go and look after her properly!

14:33.390 --> 14:34.920
<i>Why do I have to do this?</i>

14:36.130 --> 14:39.640
<i>Well, she's probably run away already.</i>

14:44.140 --> 14:47.370
<i>Did I... come to the wrong room?</i>

14:52.430 --> 14:53.710
<i>So, she's still here.</i>

14:56.270 --> 14:57.100
Hey.

14:57.100 --> 14:58.420
Leave her be.

14:58.970 --> 15:01.660
Miss Rose hasn't slept a wink.

15:01.660 --> 15:03.490
She only just fell asleep.

15:03.490 --> 15:05.840
If you have some business 
with her, come back later.

15:07.330 --> 15:11.090
She's such an admirable person!

15:11.490 --> 15:16.380
She cleaned the ward so that everyone 
would be more comfortable.

15:16.380 --> 15:19.260
Her examinations are scrupulous,
and her treatments are perfect!

15:19.260 --> 15:21.780
Wait! Did you just say "treatments"?

15:21.780 --> 15:22.730
Yes.

15:22.730 --> 15:26.600
She worked alone through 
the night to treat all of us.

15:26.600 --> 15:29.070
That's why she hasn't slept a wink.

15:29.070 --> 15:31.220
She even performed surgery on one of us!

15:31.220 --> 15:33.110
The way she wielded a 
scalpel was incredible.

15:33.110 --> 15:34.800
It was wonderful!

15:34.800 --> 15:36.600
She's an amazing person.

15:38.260 --> 15:40.590
I said to stay within your 
capabilities, didn't I?

15:41.430 --> 15:43.370
What have you done to the patients?

15:52.210 --> 15:55.900
<i>The buildup of fluid and pus is gone, 
and the opening of the wound is clean.</i>

15:56.170 --> 15:59.160
The condition of this patient's 
bedsores was severe.

15:59.160 --> 16:03.890
There was a risk of infection, 
so I excised the necrotic tissue.

16:04.160 --> 16:05.590
<i>Necrotic tissue?</i>

16:05.590 --> 16:08.890
<i>Wait, does she mean that she 
performed a debridement?</i>

16:11.250 --> 16:13.480
Which doctor helped you?

16:14.010 --> 16:17.040
None of the doctors helped me.

16:17.480 --> 16:20.170
Then, you're saying that you performed 
the treatment on your own?

16:21.050 --> 16:21.900
Yes.

16:23.950 --> 16:26.250
Do you really think I'd believe that?

16:29.400 --> 16:34.800
Doctor Graham, Miss Rose performed 
my operation on her own.

16:34.800 --> 16:36.340
You should believe her.

16:41.440 --> 16:44.000
Do you know the name of 
this patient's illness?

16:46.680 --> 16:48.600
It's bacterial pneumonia.

16:48.600 --> 16:49.910
Why do you think that?

16:50.300 --> 16:53.120
Isn't it possible that it's 
simply a buildup of fluid?

16:53.120 --> 16:58.320
Given the viscous phlegm and the increasing 
inflammation found during the exam,

16:58.910 --> 17:04.580
I felt that bacterial pneumonia was more 
likely than an accumulation of fluid.

17:07.720 --> 17:08.840
Doctor?

17:09.420 --> 17:11.530
You can return to the ward now.

17:11.530 --> 17:12.510
Yes, sir.

17:19.850 --> 17:23.490
<i>I deliberately had her examine
patients with difficult cases.</i>

17:24.000 --> 17:26.610
<i>She answered correctly every 
time, like a veteran doctor.</i>

17:32.870 --> 17:35.260
<i>Who is this girl?</i>

17:36.490 --> 17:38.120
<i>Now that I think about it...</i>

17:39.140 --> 17:42.940
<i>she spoke like an experienced 
doctor before, too, didn't she?</i>

17:44.510 --> 17:49.200
<i>But she's a young girl who's 
never attended the academy.</i>

17:49.910 --> 17:51.660
I taught myself.

17:53.090 --> 17:55.630
<i>A genius, then?</i>

18:03.670 --> 18:06.430
<i>The patients that she's been looking after</i>

18:06.430 --> 18:08.890
<i>were all abandoned by this hospital.</i>

18:11.850 --> 18:14.490
It's nice to get outside sometimes.

18:14.490 --> 18:15.360
Yes, it is.

18:16.440 --> 18:19.150
Make sure you take regular walks.

18:19.150 --> 18:21.690
It will help to get you back in shape.

18:30.500 --> 18:34.720
<i>If I'd been in her place, would I 
have been able to do what she did?</i>

18:35.320 --> 18:36.710
<i>Actually...</i>

18:37.330 --> 18:42.090
<i>is there any other doctor in the 
world who could do what she did?</i>

18:46.980 --> 18:48.410
I've got to admit defeat here.

18:49.960 --> 18:50.930
Rose.

18:51.960 --> 18:53.180
Come with me.

18:55.040 --> 18:56.690
Y-Yes, sir.

19:00.200 --> 19:02.510
Have I made a mistake somewhere?

19:02.510 --> 19:04.360
No, it's not that.

19:05.610 --> 19:08.460
It's not that, but... Well...

19:10.370 --> 19:11.720
I'm sorry.

19:11.720 --> 19:12.680
Pardon?

19:13.460 --> 19:17.140
My own prejudices made me 
see you as a nuisance.

19:18.240 --> 19:21.020
I judged you solely by appearances.

19:21.860 --> 19:23.630
I'm truly sorry for that.

19:23.630 --> 19:26.310
N-No, there's no need!

19:35.900 --> 19:38.940
Th-This is, um... you know.

19:39.330 --> 19:42.310
A handshake to seal our vow 
to be teacher and student.

19:51.290 --> 19:53.270
I look forward to working with you.

19:53.270 --> 19:57.840
As do I! I will endeavor to be even 
more diligent, Doctor Graham!

20:06.480 --> 20:08.420
<i>As I thought, it matches exactly.</i>

20:08.730 --> 20:11.620
<i>Fatigue, excessive drinking, 
excessive urination, excessive thirst...</i>

20:11.620 --> 20:13.440
<i>It's exactly what His Highness asked about.</i>

20:14.390 --> 20:17.990
Which means that His Majesty's 
illness is diabetes!

20:20.470 --> 20:23.610
But which doctor would have mentioned this?

20:25.060 --> 20:27.470
<i>Was it someone from the 
Imperial Cross Hospital?</i>

20:27.470 --> 20:30.210
<i>The empire's most brilliant 
doctors are all there,</i>

20:30.210 --> 20:32.720
<i>so it's a definite possibility.</i>

20:33.130 --> 20:36.350
<i>But when I asked before about 
His Majesty's symptoms,</i>

20:36.350 --> 20:39.830
<i>not a single one of them 
referenced this illness.</i>

20:40.920 --> 20:45.730
<i>And the doctors at Rosedale Hospital
 aren't interested in medical science.</i>

20:49.220 --> 20:52.960
It must have been a truly outstanding doctor.

20:52.960 --> 20:55.720
But where could this doctor be?!

20:57.090 --> 20:59.270
There's been word from Viscount Ven.

20:59.270 --> 21:01.740
He says he's confirmed the 
name of your illness, Father.

21:02.120 --> 21:05.540
He's currently developing a treatment plan.

21:05.540 --> 21:06.230
I see.

21:07.460 --> 21:13.630
Then, it isn't just our country that 
she's saved, it's also my health.

21:14.150 --> 21:17.090
I want to become a doctor!

21:17.090 --> 21:19.000
<i>Quite impressive.</i>

21:19.540 --> 21:25.210
<i>If Lady Elise were to become empress, then 
our Britia Empire would surely be secure.</i>

21:26.010 --> 21:29.850
<i>But if she has the talent for it...</i>

21:29.850 --> 21:34.020
<i>then would giving permission for her to 
follow the path of medicine be best?</i>

21:34.420 --> 21:38.260
Linden, where are you scheduled 
to go for the next inspection?

21:38.980 --> 21:41.270
I thought I'd go to Helan Way.

21:41.590 --> 21:45.630
What if you went to the Pierre 
Territory instead of Helan Way?

21:45.630 --> 21:49.520
That wouldn't be a problem, 
but why the Pierre Territory?

21:50.340 --> 21:53.800
Because the Teresa Hospital 
is there, isn't it?

21:55.540 --> 21:58.050
Is Lady Elise doing well there?

21:58.050 --> 22:01.830
Go and ascertain the answer to 
that question with your own eyes.

22:06.300 --> 22:10.050
The Lady Saint
